<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Klokotnitsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1230">1230</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Klokotnitsa was fought on 9 March 1230 near the village of Klokotnitsa in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-asen-ii">Ivan Asen II</a> routed the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-komnenos-doukas">Theodore Komnenos Doukas</a>, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>, who had broken a treaty and invaded Bulgaria, and took him prisoner. The victory ended Epirote power and brought much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, Macedonia and Albania under Bulgarian rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-klokotnitsa.jpg" alt="Battle of Klokotnitsa" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Klokotnitsa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
